9) From a perusal of the law laid down in the matter of Mahesh Kumar Shrivastava (supra), it appears that to declare the period of absence from duty of a public servant as dies non is punitive in nature and cannot be passed without proceeding departmentally in view of the procedure laid down under the provisions of the CCA Rules, 1966.
In the case at hand, the authority concerned straightway passed the order and declared the period of absence as dies non without affording the opportunity of hearing.
